analysisWe need to produce assert statement corresponding to comment.

The method toArray returns array of objects. The comment: "For every valid index i (from 0 up to the size of the list), if the element at index i in the list is null, then the corresponding element in the resulting array is also null; otherwise, the element in the resulting array is equal to the element in the list at index i."

We need assert after code before return? The comment is after return, but before method ends. So we need assert that captures property of array returned.

We have access to this (the list) and the returned array variable is 'array'. In spec we can refer to the returned array? Usually assert after method body can refer to \result which is the returned value. So we can write something like:

assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); (this.get(i) == null ? \result[i] == null : \result[i].equals(this.get(i)));

Need to use appropriate syntax. The element type is Object, so equality can be == for null and .equals for non-null. To be safe, we can use \result[i] == null iff this.get(i) == null, and if not null then \result[i].equals(this.get(i)). Could combine: (this.get(i) == null ? \result[i] == null : \result[i].equals(this.get(i))). That's fine.

We also need to consider that size may have changed? Use \old? No, after toArray, size unchanged. So we can use this.size().

Thus final assert: assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); (this.get(i) == null ? \result[i] == null : \result[i].equals(this.get(i)));

Make sure syntax: \result[i] is array indexing. Use parentheses.

Return final code block.

assistantfinal<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); (this.get(i) == null ? \result[i] == null : \result[i].equals(this.get(i)) );</code>
